---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import { contact, site } from '../site'
---
<Legal title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses and protects your information.`}>
  <p>This policy explains what information {site.owner} ("we") collects when you use {site.name} at <a href={site.appUrl}>{site.appUrl}</a>, and how we use it.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account details.</strong> When you sign in with GitHub or Google, we receive your account ID, display name, avatar and email address from that provider. We never see your password.</li>
    <li><strong>Content you create.</strong> Whatever you save in {site.name} is stored so the app can show it back to you.</li>
    <li><strong>Usage data.</strong> We use cookieless analytics that count page views and performance without identifying you or tracking you across sites.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>We use this information to provide and secure {site.name}, keep you signed in, and understand which features are used so we can improve them. We do not sell your personal information or use it for advertising.</p>

  <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
  <p>{site.name} runs on cloud infrastructure operated by our hosting providers, who process data on our behalf. Payments, where they apply, are handled by a payment processor; we do not store card numbers.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep your data while your account is active. When you ask us to delete your account, we delete your content and account details unless the law requires us to keep them.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>You can ask to see, correct, export or delete your information at any time: {contact}.</p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>{site.name} is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we will update the date above. Significant changes will be announced in the app.</p>
</Legal>
